# Signing keys never belong in a repository. Anyone holding one can sign an
# update that every HERMES user installs, without touching any server.
#
# `release.py` and `studio.py` keep keys in ~/.hermes-keys, outside any repo.
# These rules are the second line of defence.
#
# Note: git only treats `#` as a comment at the START of a line. A trailing
# comment makes the pattern above it useless while looking protective, so
# every comment here stays on its own line.
*.key
*.pem
keys/
.hermes-keys/
hermes

# Build output. `cargo build` and `release.py` recreate all of it, and dist/
# holds an unsigned payload.json that must never be published.
/target
/dist
.staging/

# Local scratch
rooter.origin
ARCHITECTURE.md

# Cargo.lock IS committed: this is a binary, and pinning the exact dependency
# graph is part of the supply-chain story.
